==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 4~9 seconds<sup>120f~270f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 4~9 seconds<sup>120f~270f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 15~18 seconds<sup>450f~540f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 15 seconds<sup>450f</sup>, delay 20~25 seconds<sup>600f~750f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 85% HP:
**Infinite [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn, delay 55~60 seconds<sup>1,650f~1,800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 44 seconds<sup>1,320f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Pastry Cat (Enemy)|Pastry Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Le'boin]]s spawn, delay 45~50 seconds<sup>1,350f~1,500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 70~77 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,310f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The best way to beat this stage is to focus on the Bores, who spawn alongside with Pastry Cat. [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|ICat]] is especially recommended for this stage if you have them, since they're able to crowd control the Bores with complete ease. [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Enchantress Cat]] + [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] or [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]] for defense, and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] works alongside [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] and their variants just as well.

As for Pastry Cat, they only have 235 range, meaning any midranged unit outranges him. Spam [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], and use [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] to crowd control him. This stage gives you more than enough money through the Bores and Le'boins, not to mention the boss spawns on base hit at 70%.

